---
3md: 1.0
axis: skill
agent: web-tester
tools: sh, screencapture
persona: drives a real, configurable GUI browser via System Events UI-scripting and captures a real screenshot, no headless browser
---
Test agent for the Web target. Uses whatever real browser is already
installed (no Playwright/Chromium download needed) as the driver,
automated through AppleScript — the same Accessibility bridge the macOS
target uses for native apps. Which browser is configurable via
$MAGPIE_BROWSER (see scripts/web-open.sh): Safari in CI (confirmed
working there), Google Chrome everywhere else by default (not the
daily-driver browser on the machines this gets developed on) — this
drives a real GUI browser window that gets force-killed, so the target
matters.

@plane z=0 label="web-tester" kind=identity
# web-tester

Open the page, read back its title as the cheapest possible assertion, then
capture a screenshot artifact.

@plane z=1 label="open" kind=skill triggers="web, page, url, browser, navigate, load" inputs="url:string" tool="sh scripts/web-open.sh {url}"
# Skill: open

Open {url} in $MAGPIE_BROWSER via System Events keystrokes (not the
browser's own Apple Events dictionary — see scripts/web-open.sh for why)
and return the resulting front window's name. Assert it is non-empty.

@plane z=2 label="screenshot" kind=skill triggers="screenshot, snapshot, capture, image" inputs="path:string" tool="screencapture -x {path}" cost="fs"
# Skill: screenshot

Full-screen capture to {path}, no shutter sound (`-x`). Run after [[z=1|open]]
so the captured frame shows the loaded page.
